      "description": "Watch Portland Timbers vs Seattle Sounders FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The storied rivalry between the Portland Timbers and Seattle Sounders FC added another thrilling chapter on August 2, 2026 . With both teams desperate for bragging rights in this MLS clash, the match delivered a high-octane performance that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Early Shifts and a Shock Opener The contest began with an early tactical curveball when Paul Arriola was forced off due to injury just seven minutes in, replaced by Kalani Rienzi . This sudden change didn’t dampen the visitors' spirits; in fact, it sparked them into life. In the 27th minute, it was the substitute Kalani Rienzi who broke the deadlock, firing home to give the Sounders an early lead. The physical nature of the derby soon became apparent, as Peter Kingston and Kamal Miller both went into the book before the half-hour mark as challenges flew in from both sides. Portland Strikes Back Before the Break As the first half drew to a close, the Timbers found their rhythm. Their persistence paid dividends in the 41st minute when Kristoffer Velde turned provider, delivering a pinpoint assist for Kevin Kelsy to slot home the equalizer. The goal energized the home crowd, though the intensity remained high, leading to a yellow card for Kelsy himself during a lengthy period of first-half stoppage time. The teams headed into the tunnels with the game perfectly poised at 1-1. Bye Seals the Comeback The second half saw a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked for a decisive edge. Sebastian Gomez and Antony were introduced to inject pace into the game, while the tension continued to simmer with a yellow card for Gomez in the 71st minute. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 82nd minute when David Da Costa set up Brandon Bye , who made no mistake with a clinical finish to put the Timbers ahead for the first time. Despite five minutes of added time and late pressure from Seattle, Portland held firm to secure a memorable victory in one of North America's most intense footballing environments."
